	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/prism/world/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Remodel draws the level's rock, sand and Forerunner walls from a denser model in the data folder; none comes with the game, and a level without one is drawn as Xbox. You still walk and collide on the original. Under the PRISM lightings a change bakes every level again."/>
		<string text="How far out the remodel is drawn in its full detail; beyond, its lighter far level. Low is cheaper on the graphics card."/>
		<string text="Spreads where the remodel's surfaces change to their lighter far level over a band, one by one as you move, rather than a ring of them at once."/>
		<string text="The shape Classic's sun shadows are cast from with the remodel: Far, its lighter level (the rock's ledges still shade); Full, every detail; Xbox, the map's own (cheapest)."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="In a campaign under PRISM Rebaked or Path Traced: the HQ ground, footprints and PRISM's water. Off: the ground and water as the game draws them. Never in multiplayer."/>
		<string text="HQ: sand, dirt, mud, rock, snow and ice drawn with the terrain pack's high-quality layers in the game's colours, where the pack is installed. Game's: the game's own detail."/>
		<string text="Footprints pressed into sand, snow, dirt and mud by every foot, kept for the level, where the HQ ground layers draw them."/>
		<string text="PRISM: the water's surface drawn by PRISM, its reflection traced, in the game's own colour and ripples. Game's: the game's own water. Needs a graphics card that traces rays."/>
	</strings>
</menus>
